The overlay of wineboot's per-boot keys, loaded by the in-process server
(docs/design/wine-unix.md, section 8).

No wineboot process runs, so the keys it would write at each boot (the
computer name, the hardware description with the CPU from the profile, the
volatile environment) come from native/wine/prefix/overlay.reg, which the
JS host's boot set puts at /wine/share/tempwind/overlay.reg.
- init_registry (server/registry.c) loads it right after user.reg, with its
  keys relative to \Registry, and registers no save branch for it.
- Without the file (the C harnesses other than boot), nothing is loaded.

The diff is WP4's (M2), added by the coordinator: server/* is 02xx's.

diff --git a/server/registry.c b/server/registry.c
--- a/server/registry.c
+++ b/server/registry.c
@@ -1955,6 +1955,18 @@
         fatal_error( "could not create HKEY_CURRENT_USER registry key\n" );
     free( current_user_path );
     load_init_registry_from_file( "user.reg", hkcu );
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+    /* Tempwind (wine-unix.md, section 8): the overlay of wineboot's per-boot
+     * keys, relative to \Registry. Loaded only: it is no save branch. */
+    {
+        FILE *f = fopen( "/wine/share/tempwind/overlay.reg", "r" );
+        if (f)
+        {
+            load_keys( root_key, "overlay.reg", f, 0 );
+            fclose( f );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
 
     /* set the shared flag on Software\Classes\Wow6432Node for all platforms */
     for (i = 1; i < supported_machines_count; i++)
